Our tables — CC BY 4.0
-----------------------------
Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International. You may share and adapt the
data, including commercially, provided you give appropriate credit, link to the
licence, and indicate whether changes were made. Full text:
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

Attribution should name the release id and the model versions listed in
README.md, so a reader can obtain the same rows.

Knowledge-base facts — CC0 1.0 (Wikidata facts); per-row licence for portrait URLs
--------------------------------------
Biographical and office-holding facts sourced from a public collaborative
knowledge base are released under CC0 1.0 Universal, matching their upstream
terms. Full text: https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/

Portrait columns are a URL, a credit string and a per-row image licence. **No
image file is redistributed in this release.** Before reusing a portrait, read
that row's own licence at the source; it is frequently more restrictive than the
facts beside it.

Documentation — CC BY 4.0
--------------------------------
README.md, DATA_DICTIONARY.md and CHANGELOG.md are CC BY 4.0.

Not covered by this licence
---------------------------
Model weights, prompts and lexicons are not published. Their SHA-256
fingerprints are, and they appear on every row they produced.

Third-party editorial text — headlines and feed-written summaries — is not in
this release and is not licensed by it. `events_metadata` carries `source_url`;
follow it to the publisher and read their terms.

No warranty
-----------
The data is provided as-is, without warranty of any kind. Values are readings of
observed conditions at each row's own timestamp. They are not forecasts, not
advice, and not a statement about what will happen.
